      "raw_response": " A. Nothing in particular happens if you leave your phone charging past 100%.\n\nModern smartphones have built-in mechanisms to prevent overcharging. Once the battery reaches 100%, the power adapter reduces the current to trickle charging to conserve battery life and prevent damage (Source: TechRadar, accessed 2021).\n\nB and C are incorrect because they suggest negative consequences that are not supported by the technology used in modern smartphones.\n\nD is only partially correct. While it's true that frequently charging and discharging your phone can degrade the battery's lifespan, leaving it charging past 100% will not cause immediate and permanent damage (Source: Battery University, accessed 2021). However, repeatedly charging your phone to 100% and then letting it drain completely can shorten the battery's lifespan over time.\n\nANSWER: A",
